---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---
<Base title="About" description="Why Open Repair Record exists, who started it, and how it is licensed." section="about">
  <div class="wrap page-head">
    <div class="prose">
      <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
      <h1>Why this exists</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        A slow repair is frustrating. A repair marked "done" that nobody checked is worse: the resident finds out when
        the problem comes back, and the record says everything was fine.
      </p>
      <p>
        Repair systems are good at moving a ticket from open to closed. They are less good at recording what that
        closing means: who said the work was done, what was checked, and whether the person who reported the problem
        agrees. Open Repair Record is a small, shared answer to that: a guide to what a completed repair should say,
        and a free tool that helps write it.
      </p>

      <h2>Who is behind it</h2>
      <p>
        Open Repair Record was initiated by the team behind <a href="https://pmfriend.com/">PMFriend</a>, the AI bridge
        between property management and facility management. PMFriend automates the whole repair loop, from the first
        message to the resident's confirmation, and the work around it, from compliance certificates to owner reports.
        The guide and this tool are deliberately useful without it: no account, no PMFriend footer on your reports,
        and anyone, including other software vendors, is welcome to use and implement the format.
      </p>

      <h2>Licences</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>The guide, the template and the examples: <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/">Creative Commons Attribution 4.0</a>. Credit "Open Repair Record, openrepairrecord.com".</li>
        <li>The builder's code and the JSON Schema: MIT.</li>
        <li>The examples are fictional. Any resemblance to real people, companies or addresses is coincidental.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Taking part</h2>
      <p>
        The format is at version 0.1 and will change with use. If you run maintenance, do repairs, or build software for
        either, we would like to see a real (anonymised) completion report and hear what this gets wrong. Write to
        <a href="mailto:support@pmfriend.com">support@pmfriend.com</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
